      "id": 1,
      "text": "Fieldale was founded in 1916 when Marshall Field & Company bought land from the Waller heirs and built Fieldcrest Mills.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fieldale%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s original company clubhouse, 8,500 sq ft, still stands and is listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fieldale%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Fieldale’s historic district, centered on the Smith River, remains remarkably intact, showcasing a classic early‑20th‑century company town layout.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.dhr.virginia.gov/historic-registers/044-5173/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1930, unmarried female workers lived in the Virginia Home while men stayed in the Fieldale Hotel, reflecting the era’s gendered housing.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.dhr.virginia.gov/historic-registers/044-5173/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Smith River’s Jordan Creek tributary runs through the village’s center, named after Jordan Hairston, a local pioneer.",
